## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/worleynoise.html
- Summary (EN): Generates Worley (cellular) noise by measuring distances to a set of points on a grid, useful for cell-like textures. For world-space positions, use Worley Noise 3D. Output: the noise layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère un bruit cellulaire de Worley en 2D à partir de distances à une grille de points, avec taille, gigue, métrique et post-traitement réglables.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: reference layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "pos (optional): UV layer that replaces the pixel's image coordinates as the noise source"]

- Key parameters: ["Type Info: type information for the output layer", "Element Size: size of the basic noise cell in image coordinates; Element Scale adjusts it per axis when Per-Component Controls is on", "Jitter: random offset of each grid point before distances are measured; Jitter Scale adjusts it per axis", "Lattice Type: square (rectangular) grid or simplicial grid (hexagonal cells)", "Metric: Euclidean (circular cells), Manhattan (diamond), Chebyshev (square)", "Round Border: smooths cell borders, Euclidean only", "Offset: shifts the whole noise pattern", "Tile Size: repeat size so the noise can tile", "Post Processing, applied in order: Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["The page warns that values greater than 1 may produce artifacts because they jitter past the search radius", "Complement assumes values between 0 and 1, so results can go out of range with other inputs"]

